ld (#fd9a), a (0x4015): Store the value in register A (0xC3) into memory address 0xFD9A. Address 0xFD9A is part of the MSX hooks area, specifically the HKEYI hook, which is used for custom interrupt handling.

ld hl, #4044 (0x4018): Load the value 0x4044 into the HL register pair. This could be an address or data, depending on the context of the code.

ld (#fd9b), hl (0x401B): Store the value in the HL register pair (0x4044) into memory address 0xFD9B. This address is immediately after the HKEYI hook, and the data might be related to the custom interrupt handler.
